A||N||24||William||Macco troubles||||9||
Z||000000||William||02-20-2000||02:52 PM||||OK, here goes. Just got my car back from Macco with a new paint job. I'm not going to show the car so I didn't want a 1500 dollar paint job. I crossed my fingers and went for there 1/2 off sale. Well the paint job was great. They matched the orignal red perfect and the car looks brand new again. It looks as good as any factory paint I have seen. Once I got home and put on the ANAL cap I noticed some problems. looks like there was some grains of sand on the car when it was painted. about 15 or so in various locations.<BR>I'm not sure what to do now, should I take it back? the little bumps are not seen until you start to really inspect close. Is this unaccetable even for a 500.00 paint job? It looks so good overall that I'm afraid they might ruin it all because I'm too picky. Would they just spot repair it and ruin the otherwise nice job? It would appear that to do it right, the whole car would need to be redone, and because I paid so little I'm afraid I would have to sue them. I would have to say that it doesn't look that bad to me but I would not want other people pointing it out a shaking there head. Should I be happy it looks so good overall or should I complain and perhaps get a car back that could look worse? Input please.||||reg||9
Z||000001||wkayl||02-20-2000||02:57 PM||||My son's GT he just got has a Macco job from about 4 months ago by the previous owner.  We are going to wet sand it when the weather is warmer.  Untill then, we just stand back about 50 feet to admire it.||||reg||1
Z||000002||William||02-20-2000||03:04 PM||||OK, that tells me that overall I may have gotten lucky and had better not let them touch it again. I'm working on getting a pic today to post||||reg||1
