Z||000013||mutfish||02-20-2000||08:17 PM||||If your only complaint is a few specks of dirt in a $500 macco paint job,you should drop to your knees,fold your hands together and thank the lord for smiling down on you and your fiero.........||||reg||1
Z||000014||batboy||02-20-2000||09:13 PM||||William, you need to chat with Cooter, he's one of our painting experts. But like was mentioned a couple times already, somebody really good at wet sanding can probably take care of those minor imperfections. I've seen more expensive paint jobs than that turn out worse. There was a topic a couple months ago about paint and whether or not to use a flex agent, but I forgot what was said. I've heard Cooter say that taking off the panels makes it really easy for the guy shooting the paint, but it's also really easy to scratch or ding the fresh paint during reassembly.||||reg||1
Z||000015||BENGAL4||02-20-2000||10:00 PM||||I got my car painted at Maaco last summer. They did a pretty good job. Their disclaimer is that it is production painting. I had them paint the spoiler seperate from the rest of the car. There was alot of overspray and I cleaned up most of it. I keep finding more, every time I wax it. I have noticed some cracking in the front and rear facia's though. I did not tell them to add a flexing agent. I assumed that they would do it automaticly. They do not. I also knew going in that there would be some imperfections in the paint. They state this on the invoice you sign. All in all, you get what you pay for. They put a new front facia, right and left ground effects, and new 1/4 window plus painted the car, for $800.00 dollars ( I bought all the body parts). I am going to have a forum members dad, repaint it this summer. Finally, if you are on a tight budget, by all means, take it to Maaco. I would just ask about a flexing agent.||||reg||1
Z||000016||Monkeyman||02-20-2000||11:40 PM||||I can attest to the fact that Bills paint looks good.  I remember the crack in the front fascia paint now.  It is a nice paint  job.  I didn't even know it was from Maaco.  ||||reg||1
Z||000017||SloPonti||02-20-2000||11:51 PM||||i would strogly recommend staying away from macco!!!! i had my girlfriends camaro painted there about three years ago! i was going to do the body work myself but they said they would not warranty the work if i did so we paid them to do all body work! we got the car back and they had skipped some of the rust spots and just painted over them! i took back the car and complained and they told me that i did not say which spots i wanted fixed! gee i only told them that i wanted the all the body work done! who in there right mine would only fix half the body work and then paint a car! not me so anyways they repainted it for free but they charged me for the extra body work! now three months after that the paint was flaking off and the rust has come back so i took it back in and they told me it was road debrit that coused the car to flake off and about the rust they said they did not warrenty the body work! i guess you get what you paid for!<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000018||stimpy||02-21-2000||12:16 AM||||OK... note to self. make sure to point out all body rust to Maaco folks before they paint Fiero.||||reg||1
Z||000019||SN1PERVII||02-21-2000||01:14 AM||||stimpy you arent serious right??||||reg||1
Z||000020||fierodave||02-21-2000||05:33 AM||||<BR>OK  my 2 cents now  lol  flame suit on!!!   <P>As you know I am doing the Indy right now bc/cc Dupont.  <BR>BUT  I have a good friend who owns one the maaco shops here in town!  the work is as good as the people doing   the work! <P>They don't have Maaco elves running from maaco to maaco painting cars :~) That  said!!!<BR>Now  If you wanted me to paint your car the way I did the Indy  for $500.00  I would  laugh you right out of the shop!!!!   MY materials for the INdy at my cost!!  was close to $500.00  the job I am getting done to this car at a local high end body shop would have been $2,500.00 time and materials,(also had front repair)  <BR>So  if you are worried about a little dirt,  like it was said above  count your blessings.<P>My paint has dirt in it!  <BR>all paint jobs will have dirt in it,  The factory had dirt in the paint!<P>It is my opinion you shouldn't rip on maaco,  there not all the same!  and you get what you pay for too!<P>And yes,  I have had maaco jobs done!<BR>I have had 9 cars done to date,  <BR>two where Fiero's  and they both look x-lint to this day!  and one has two winters on it, in the snow and salt and gets washed once a week,  <BR>but I did wet sand and buff it out after 3 weeks time  <BR>The intergrated clear is just an old acrylic enamel hardner paint job with 90's materials.<P>SO  you get what you pay for!  <BR>you should check out the shop before you get the work done!  ask for customer names, and call them.........  ask them if they like the job!!!  <BR>PLease guys don't condem all maaco's sorry for the long one  just HAD to kick in here.  btw  flex agents used in the fiero( at the factory) where used because the cars body panels were put on after the car was assembled, they needed the flex so the panels did not get cracks with the assembly.  and as all good painters know!!!!!!!   most flex agents will pop there ther nut!!! (dry up in 3 to 6 months anyway)   plus!  a flex agent comes with the cost of being a bit more dull in the finish department compared to not useing one at all, Most all modern urethane paints are more flexible than the stuff with the agent added anyway!   thanks for the space<BR>FD||||reg||10
Z||000021||stimpy||02-21-2000||07:10 AM||||Haven't seen anybody rot on my Fiero <BR>yet. But do you think they can take <BR>out those little grocery cart dings? :rolleyes||||reg||1
Z||000022||William||02-21-2000||09:27 AM||||I personally never ripped on Macco. I was quite shocked that it looked as good as it did for the money. Part of the cost was for the black out and a complete strip of the hood and roof due to paint cracking. Get this now, I got there Supreme level paint at half off so the cost just for the paint job itself was $249.00. After reading all the posts I've have decided to live with the paint job and enjoy the now NEW looking car.If the bumps start to bother me, I may try the wet sanding one day. As for now, I've saved $1000.00 and that puts me alot closer to a new crate engine. I still would not recommend your average Macco for a high level show car. But for $249.00, all you guys driving old faded daily drivers should jump on this sale while it lasts. Theres no reason to see that old paint when your fiero could look new again fot this price!!!!!!||||reg||7
Z||000023||Monkeyman||02-21-2000||01:11 PM||||stimpy--you need to put another colon (or is it a semi-colon?  I never can remember which is which) after the ":rolleyes" to get the smilies to work.||||reg||1
Z||000024||Ed||02-21-2000||09:01 PM||||Fierodave: Didn't Bill K. get his car painted at Macco? <P>I posted here about a month ago about our club president who had his Formula painted at Macco. I remarked at that time that it looked really good, in metallic green.  So, I'd have to agree with others who have good results.  Looks like the thing to do is shop around a see examples of the work any particular shop does.  ||||reg||1
